---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---
<Layout title="Now Playing" description="See what song is currently playing at the Draper Family Light Show.">
  <section class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 py-16 text-center">
    <h1 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-extrabold text-midnight mb-4">Now Playing</h1>
    <p class="text-slate-600 mb-8">
      Here's what song is playing at the show right now, pulled live from our Remote Falcon display.
    </p>

    <div class="rounded-xl overflow-hidden shadow-lg bg-white">
      <embed
        type="text/html"
        src="https://draperlightshow.remotefalcon.com/remote-falcon"
        width="100%"
        height="300"
      />
    </div>

    <!--
      NOTE FOR FUTURE YOU: this embeds Remote Falcon just to show the current song title.
      If you'd rather build your own lightweight "Now Playing" widget straight from FPP's
      status API (e.g. GET /api/fppd/status on your FPP box) instead of embedding a whole
      Remote Falcon page, that's very doable — see the README for a sketch of how that could work.
    -->
  </section>
</Layout>
